  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.29,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "Undiluted readings doubled about every hour from 0 to 5 h (0.016 to 0.58), then stopped suddenly at about 0.90 and stayed flat (0.88–0.95) from 6 to 18 h. That pattern suggests the reader hit its upper limit, not that growth stopped. Diluted 18 h aliquot: 10× gave 0.3226 and 0.3335 (×10 ≈ 3.28); 50× gave 0.0653 and 0.0660 (×50 ≈ 3.29). The two dilutions agree after scaling, so the reader is proportional in the diluted range, and the true OD at 18 h is about 3.3, roughly 3.6 times the undiluted reading. The 12 h aliquot at 10× gave 0.3189 and 0.3400 (≈3.3), so biomass was already about 3.3 by 12 h and stayed there. This is a real stationary phase at about OD 3.3, not 0.9. The undiluted readings across the final hours therefore underestimate biomass because the reader saturates."
  },
